233
00:15:44,252 --> 00:15:47,690
I have no reason to treat
you poorly. Also.

234
00:15:48,490 --> 00:15:51,160
But I get the sense
you and I are similar.

235
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:55,108
What do you mean?
Well, your mother's

236
00:15:55,192 --> 00:15:58,870
name was Emma Helford, correct?
You've heard of her?

237
00:16:00,390 --> 00:16:02,928
Yes. In fact,
I met Madam Halford

238
00:16:03,012 --> 00:16:05,550
when I was only about
4 or 5 years old.

239
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:08,158
I was surprised
to find out there

240
00:16:08,242 --> 00:16:10,480
was a woman.
Silver sugar master.

241
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:14,470
You meant mama.

242
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:18,820
You see,
I'm the son of Edward Powell.

243
00:16:19,330 --> 00:16:22,270
Silver sugar master.
Just like your mother.

244
00:16:22,990 --> 00:16:28,810
Wait a minute. Edward Powell.
Right. Previous Viscount?

245
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:31,918
Indeed.
Thanks to him, I met a lot

246
00:16:32,002 --> 00:16:35,710
of silver sugar masters,
including Alf Hingley.

247
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:38,488
My mother told me
he was a wonderful

248
00:16:38,572 --> 00:16:41,980
silver sugar viscount who
served for over 20 years.

249
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:47,330
And if I recall, about six
months before mama passed away.

250
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:51,938
Sickness took him.
He may well have been wonderful,

251
00:16:52,022 --> 00:16:56,150
but I wouldn't have known that back
when my father was Viscount.

252
00:16:56,450 --> 00:16:58,178
There was a year like this where

253
00:16:58,262 --> 00:17:00,440
the sugar apple
harvest was lacking.

254
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:03,338
Apparently there was
a great deal of chaos.

255
00:17:03,452 --> 00:17:05,738
My father always
regretted that year.

256
00:17:05,852 --> 00:17:08,780
I believe your father came from the
page school. Isn't that right?

257
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:11,628
So why are you
with the Radcliffe School?

258
00:17:11,742 --> 00:17:15,228
Because if I'd enrolled with Paige, they'd
have given me special treatment.

259
00:17:15,312 --> 00:17:18,630
Since I'm Paul's son.
I hated that idea.

260
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:22,800
So I came here where I'd be
just like any other artisan.

261
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:27,150
That's what I thought, at least.
But it's not all that different.

262
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,388
I respected my father,
but my situation

263
00:17:30,472 --> 00:17:33,328
was terribly restrictive
and I couldn't participate

264
00:17:33,412 --> 00:17:35,848
in the exhibition as long
as he was alive.

265
00:17:35,962 --> 00:17:39,238
Why not? Because if
I had received the Royal Medal,

266
00:17:39,322 --> 00:17:41,488
the critics would have
spread gossip about me.

267
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:44,008
They'd say the Royal
family favored me because

268
00:17:44,092 --> 00:17:46,468
I was the son
of the silver sugar viscount.

269
00:17:46,552 --> 00:17:48,238
And if I hadn't won, they'd have

270
00:17:48,322 --> 00:17:51,160
judged me for failing in
spite of who my father was.

271
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:58,088
I couldn't risk his reputation.
But the mourning period is over,

272
00:17:58,172 --> 00:18:00,548
which means as of this year,
I should be

273
00:18:00,632 --> 00:18:02,630
able to compete
in the exhibition.

274
00:18:03,730 --> 00:18:07,778
Are. Anyway,
I thought I'd work on my piece

275
00:18:07,862 --> 00:18:10,508
for a bit today.
This shall. In your room?

276
00:18:10,622 --> 00:18:14,528
Um, yes. If you ask him, then
I'm sure he'll be glad to help

277
00:18:14,612 --> 00:18:18,770
you. Excellent.
Well, then, good luck.

278
00:18:21,290 --> 00:18:25,298
Keith isn't letting his circumstances hold him
back from doing his best.

279
00:18:25,382 --> 00:18:30,210
So I can't either.
I won't let him beat me.

280
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:37,868
I'm sorry for the early hour.
I did make

281
00:18:37,952 --> 00:18:40,040
a promise, so I'll keep it.

282
00:18:40,430 --> 00:18:42,728
Shall I do a trick?
Take off my clothes,

283
00:18:42,812 --> 00:18:45,968
perhaps.
Give your orders, boy. Quickly.

284
00:18:46,082 --> 00:18:49,700
Boy. All right. It appears we're
about the same age, though.

285
00:18:50,030 --> 00:18:52,178
Could you go stand
by that window? There.

286
00:18:52,262 --> 00:18:54,668
That should be great.
I want to get

287
00:18:54,752 --> 00:18:56,930
a good sense of your
air and appearance.

288
00:18:58,130 --> 00:19:00,968
It's too bad for Anne.
She just got here,

289
00:19:01,052 --> 00:19:04,238
and the rest of us already
refined all the sugar we need.

290
00:19:04,322 --> 00:19:06,350
I hope she
prepared ahead of time.

291
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:09,068
Not at all.
In fact, your schoolmates

292
00:19:09,182 --> 00:19:12,830
neglected to tell her what
happened this year. Lucky you.

293
00:19:14,210 --> 00:19:18,008
They didn't tell her.
Selfish cowards. The

294
00:19:18,092 --> 00:19:21,200
lot of them.
It's downright disgraceful.

295
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:26,358
That upsets me.
But I'm glad that

296
00:19:26,442 --> 00:19:28,530
Ann is entering
the exhibition anyway.

297
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,308
If it were only
the artisans from here,

298
00:19:31,392 --> 00:19:34,080
I wouldn't have
any competition to speak of.

299
00:19:34,550 --> 00:19:37,928
Rumor has it the royal medal's
going to Sammy this time.

300
00:19:38,012 --> 00:19:40,670
But if you ask me,
he isn't even worth a mention.

301
00:19:41,030 --> 00:19:45,998
Jonas is capable enough, but his work
is missing a crucial element.

302
00:19:46,112 --> 00:19:48,950
I've been waiting for an
opponent with equal skill,

303
00:19:49,130 --> 00:19:51,830
so she's going to make
it worthwhile for me.

304
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:56,408
Also.
This is probably the only time

305
00:19:56,492 --> 00:19:59,180
I'll get to compete against
Anne at the exhibition.

306
00:19:59,390 --> 00:20:01,970
This year will be
Anne's final chance.

307
00:20:02,090 --> 00:20:03,860
It is a great honour for me.

308
00:20:04,770 --> 00:20:09,068
It's her final chance.
That's right. If she

309
00:20:09,152 --> 00:20:11,750
can't become a silver
sugar master this time.

310
00:20:12,890 --> 00:20:14,690
Then she can never become one.

311
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:19,230
Everyone's too jealous of her.

312
00:20:19,470 --> 00:20:21,978
There was last year's contest.
Then all

313
00:20:22,062 --> 00:20:24,840
that business involving
the former Duke of Phylax.

314
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:27,168
Even if this had been a normal

315
00:20:27,252 --> 00:20:29,928
year when artisans could
harvest their own sugar apples,

316
00:20:30,012 --> 00:20:32,520
they still would have hindered
her in some way.

317
00:20:33,210 --> 00:20:35,658
I'd say this was
a stroke of good fortune,

318
00:20:35,742 --> 00:20:39,300
because working with us will
guarantee her some silver sugar.

319
00:20:40,060 --> 00:20:41,980
But it won't
happen again this way.

320
00:20:42,490 --> 00:20:45,400
She'll never be able to get
the supplies she needs.

321
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:50,868
That said, you mustn't tell her.
I don't

322
00:20:50,952 --> 00:20:53,130
want her to feel
that additional pressure.

323
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:56,710
I'd rather compete
with her fairly.

